/P 143 0 R
/E (Why Not Tree-Based Models?)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [32]
>>
endobj
292 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 143 0 R
/E (Once the non-isothermal temperature correction is applied, the underlying yield surface as a function of the  features is smooth. Tree-based models approximate smooth functions with axis-aligned step splits. With only 150 samples, they lack the data needed to approximate smooth curves accurately without overfitting.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [33]
>>
endobj
293 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 143 0 R
/E (Why Bagged Multi Level Perceptron?)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [34]
>>
endobj
294 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 143 0 R
/E (A small Multi-Layer Perceptron  with smooth ReLU activations naturally captures continuous physical relationships better than decision trees on small datasets. Using the L-BFGS solver for reliable convergence, the model ensembles 15 independently seeded networks  to apply bagging principles, eliminating weight-initialization variance and stabilizing final predictions. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [35]
>>
endobj
