438 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (Across different environments, the same pipeline produced slightly different predictions despite consistent overall trends. This was attributed to numerical differences arising from NumPy, SciPy, scikit-learn, and BLAS implementations)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [21]
>>
endobj
439 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (Root Cause Analysis:)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
440 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (The source of the reproducibility issue was isolated to the neural-network stage of the pipeline.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
441 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (Even when near-identical mechanistic parameters were supplied to the MLP, the resulting predictions could differ substantially. More importantly, introducing an extremely small relative perturbation of only \(10^{-12}\) into the MLP inputs resulted huge changes.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
442 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (Why the MLP behaves this way)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [25]
>>
endobj
443 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (The \(16,8\) MLP has ~481 trainable parameters for only 150 observations, achieving a very low training RMSE . This near-interpolation, combined with 2000 LBFGS iterations and no early stopping, makes predictions highly sensitive to tiny numerical differences during optimization. As a result, different environments can converge to different weight configurations with similar training performance but different test predictions. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [26]
>>
endobj
444 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (Impact on Reproducibility)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [27]
>>
endobj
445 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (The model's validation metrics and mechanistic parameters are substantially more stable than its exact test predictions. The cross-validation RMSE and the fitted mechanistic parameters were reproducible, whereas the exact leaderboard prediction values were sensitive to the numerical environment.  Exact reproduction of the submitted predictions cannot be guaranteed across different numerical environments.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [28]
>>
endobj
